Ostia third-party notices
=========================

Ostia's own code is licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE and NOTICE).
This file lists the third-party software Ostia uses, as approved by RFC-0001 §2.3
(docs/rfcs/0001-m0-foundations.md), with how each is used and when it is integrated.

"Vendored" means the source is copied into this repository. "Fetched" means CPM
downloads a pinned release at build time (RFC-0001 §2.4). "System" means the build
finds an existing installation. "dlopen" means it is loaded at runtime and never
linked or bundled. Full license texts are included here for vendored code and for
code the topology model compiles in or links (nlohmann/json, hwloc); they are added
for any other component before a binary release that bundles it (PRD, Third-party
code).

